  "step_3": "The decision reason requires calculating an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes (2333.33) and comparing each lottery based on the probability of exceeding this level. However, the individual does not refer to any such calculation or reference point. Instead, the individual focuses on the certainty of Lottery A (100% win) and avoidance of risk (no chance of loss). While both the reason and the individual prefer Lottery A, the justification differs: the reason relies on probabilistic superiority over an aspiration level, whereas the individual relies on risk aversion and certainty. There is no evidence that the individual computed or considered the mean of all outcomes or evaluated how often each lottery exceeds that value. Therefore, the cognitive process described does not align with the decision reason, even though the final preference is the same.",
  "final_assessment_score": 20
}

